From: SushyDev <mail@sushy.dev>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:20:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ASoC: qcom: q6apm: don't report a stale state as ready

q6apm_get_apm_state() ignores the result of the state query and returns
apm->state, which still holds the previous answer when the command times
out; an allocation failure becomes a negative errno, which the bool
q6apm_is_adsp_ready() reads as true. Either way q6prm probes against an
ADSP that is not ready. Report not-ready on any failure so probe defers.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
index f167b9d..d694fa7 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
@@ -145,9 +145,11 @@ static int q6apm_get_apm_state(struct q6apm *apm)
 	struct gpr_pkt *pkt __free(kfree) = audioreach_alloc_apm_cmd_pkt(0,
 								APM_CMD_GET_SPF_STATE, 0);
 	if (IS_ERR(pkt))
-		return PTR_ERR(pkt);
+		return 0;
 
-	q6apm_send_cmd_sync(apm, pkt, APM_CMD_RSP_GET_SPF_STATE);
+	/* A timeout leaves the last answer in apm->state, which may say ready. */
+	if (q6apm_send_cmd_sync(apm, pkt, APM_CMD_RSP_GET_SPF_STATE))
+		return 0;
 
 	return apm->state;
 }
